class.description:
[TTSPersonaSettingsServer] is the settings domain [code]"tts_personas"[/code]: it stores the [TTSPersona]s the player created or changed (voice, language, volume, pitch, rate, interrupt) and the player's default persona, loads them when the game starts and applies them to [TTSServer] (in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_PHASE_SERVERS]).
The personas of the game stay unchanged. The player's personas are applied as [i]persona overrides[/i] ([method TTSServer.set_persona_override], [method TTSServer.set_default_persona_override]): [method TTSServer.get_persona], [method TTSServer.speak_with_persona] and the default persona see the player's version first, even if the game adds its personas later (for example in [method Node._ready]). Removing the player's version ([method remove_persona], [method SettingsServer.reset_to_defaults]) brings the game's persona back. The defaults of this domain are empty: only what the player created or changed is stored.
The settings resource is a [TTSPersonaListSettings] with one [TTSPersonaSettings] entry per persona, identified by [member TTSPersonaSettings.persona_name]. The default persona is the entry with [member TTSPersonaSettings.default] set, so the resource holds nothing but the list: with [member ProjectSettings.settings/general/default_format], or the format of the domain group [code]settings/<domain>/[/code], set to [constant ResourceTextSerializer.FORMAT_CSV], the file [code]user://settings/tts_personas.csv[/code] has one row per persona. The default file is [code]user://settings/tts_personas.ini[/code].
A stored voice that does not exist on the current device is kept (it may exist on the player's other device). [TTSServer] picks another voice then (see [method TTSServer.resolve_voice_id]), a warning is printed once per persona and voice, and [method get_missing_voice_personas] returns the persona, so an options menu can show it.
The typed methods below go through [method ListSettingsServer.set_entry_value] or [method ListSettingsServer.add_entry]: in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_MODE_IMMEDIATE] a change reaches [TTSServer] at once and is saved at the end of the frame; in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_MODE_MANUAL] it waits for [method SettingsServer.apply].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _ready():
	# The game's persona, shipped with the game.
	var narrator = TTSPersona.new()
	narrator.persona_name = &"narrator"
	narrator.language = "en"
	TTSServer.add_persona(narrator)

# Options menu: the player makes the narrator faster and chooses it as default.
func _on_rate_slider_value_changed(value):
	TTSPersonaSettingsServer.set_persona_value(&"narrator", &"rate", value)
	TTSPersonaSettingsServer.set_default_persona(&"narrator")

func speak_line(text):
	TTSServer.speak_with_persona(text, &"narrator") # Uses the player's narrator.
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public override void _Ready()
{
    // The game's persona, shipped with the game.
    var narrator = new TtsPersona();
    narrator.PersonaName = "narrator";
    narrator.Language = "en";
    TtsServer.AddPersona(narrator);
}

// Options menu: the player makes the narrator faster and chooses it as default.
private void OnRateSliderValueChanged(double value)
{
    TtsPersonaSettingsServer.SetPersonaValue("narrator", "rate", value);
    TtsPersonaSettingsServer.SetDefaultPersona("narrator");
}

private void SpeakLine(string text)
{
    TtsServer.SpeakWithPersona(text, "narrator"); // Uses the player's narrator.
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] On the Web, the browser loads its voice list asynchronously. When the settings are applied at startup, the list is usually still empty: no voice is reported missing then and the browser chooses the voice. Call [method get_missing_voice_personas] again later, for example when the options menu opens.
